experiment: ctxfour
  SHORT RUN — 200000 ticks against a minimum of 3400000. derived: ctxself's session at FOUR words. partprobe cleared the index at
  four (0.895 vs chance 0.250); this asks whether the BIAS holds four
  mappings on one reward channel. Oracle arm only -- if a perfect index
  cannot carry four, the creature's own cannot either. Refuses unless
  ctx_match reads 1.000, which is the k-way assignment's own check
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  instrument        ctxfour   trial seed 000000000135672c   71 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `partprobe` cleared the INDEX at four words (0.895
                    against chance 0.250). Can the BIAS hold four
                    mappings on one reward channel?
  the prediction    4 contexts is 2x the parameters of 2, so ~2x the
                    trials: at 6.8M expect what two words gave at 3.4M,
                    ~65 Hz spread and ~0.80 direction (chance 0.250).
  the oracle arm    the host writes the index, so this is the CEILING.
                    If a perfect index cannot carry four, the creature's
                    own cannot either.

